0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I don't think that issue title is the best, but easier to show with code:\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n  \r\nclass A {\r\n \r\n  public function test(): stdClass\r\n  {\r\n    $user = 'jane';\r\n    \r\n    $status = $this->check($user);\r\n    if ($status !== true) {\r\n      // Will only be stdClass here, not `true`\r\n      return $status;\r\n    }\r\n   \r\n    $status = new stdClass();\r\n    return $status;\r\n  }\r\n  \r\n  /**\r\n   * @return stdClass|true\r\n   */\r\n  public function check(string $user)\r\n  {\r\n   \t if ($user === 'carl') {\r\n      \treturn true; \r\n     } else {\r\n        return new stdClass();\r\n     }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `check` method only returns `stdClass` or `true`, but if I check that a variable that holds that return `!== true` psalm doesn't seem to remove `true` as a possible return type in the `test` method.\r\n\r\nhttps://getpsalm.org/r/f70e9e8818","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"h